       "dsh2o_dt_total"
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "cold_A1_frozen_column",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy COLD-SEASON single-column run, data/eqwefic/noahcold_scm, dumped by ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-noahcold and replayed through the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) kernels/noah_driver at ESM_DT = 0.01 s. THE ASSERTED CLAIM is that the SUM of the two mounted tendencies reproduces WRF's own step: `dsh2o_dt_total` against (sh2o_out - sh2o_in)/dt, `dsmc_dt_total` against (smc_out - smc_in)/dt, and `dsice_dt` against the ice difference, all per layer. WRF forms none of these; it advances the water with SMFLX and then applies HRT's phase-change sink to what SMFLX has already moved, so this is a statement about the two components TOGETHER. THE REFERENCE STEP WAS CHOSEN BY MEASURING ITS V, not by assuming smaller is better (the rule is FORTRAN_BUGS N99 / PLAN section 6: a differenced reference HAS a cancellation floor, so its accuracy is a V in dt and the step is the minimum). Worst absolute residual over this document's assertions, at the three replay passes: 3.405e-11 at ESM_DT = 1e-6 s, 4.653e-15 at 0.01 s, 6.148e-15 at 60 s. The left branch is pure cancellation -- the liquid-water increment is only 1.6e-12 of sh2o at 1e-6 s, so the reference difference keeps about four digits, and the residual scales as 1/dt (a 10000x drop in dt raises it by 9000x). The right branch is the operator-splitting error plus WRF's interval clamp; on THIS column the clamp does not flip and 60 s costs only a factor of 1.3, but over the seventeen cold bare-ground columns the clamp decision flips at one layer of SIX of them at 60 s (0 -> 2, stopped at `free`), which turns the phase term into a finite-step artefact rather than a rate -- exactly the bind FORTRAN_BUGS N97 describes. 0.01 s is the minimum and it is four orders better than either end. TOLERANCES ARE THE REFERENCE'S FLOOR, NOT THE ASSEMBLY'S ACCURACY, and they are ABSOLUTE for a traced reason: the smallest layer tendency is 2.6e-12 per second while the top layer's is 3.8e-07, so a single relative bound would be meaningless. The floor is eps(sh2o)/dt = 2.2e-16 x 0.3 / 0.01 = 6.7e-15 per second; the measured worst residual over the three documents is 4.7e-15, i.e. AT that floor, and the published bound of 1e-14 is 2.1x it. The phase rate itself is asserted at abs 1e-18 and is exact, because it is referenced against the N97 publisher rather than any difference. `phase_active` and `supersaturation_active` are asserted at ZERO tolerance. THIS COLUMN: case A step 1, the only step in the whole cold reference set that takes the ACTIVE branch of the frozen-ground infiltration reduction (column ice 0.19 m against the 1e-2 m threshold), and one whose water supply is DEW rather than precipitation -- NOPAC adds the dew to the precipitation before the canopy split, so the column gains water with no rain at all. A different transport regime, on a different case, which is why it is a separate document rather than another assertion on the same one. It also carries the largest residual of the three, 4.7e-15, which is the number the 1e-14 bound is set from.",
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "smcmax0": 0.47600001096725464,
      "bexp0": 5.329999923706055,
      "edir0": 0.0,
      "ec0": 0.0,
      "etp0": -18.454618195736202,
      "prcp0": 0.0,
      "shdfac0": 0.5,
      "cmc0": 0.0,
      "smcwlt0": 0.08399999886751175,
      "dksat0": 2.8100000690756133e-06,
      "dwsat0": 2.390000008745119e-05,
      "kdt0": 4.215000114255272,
      "frzx0": 0.17460114362402857,
      "slope0": 0.10000000149011612,
      "tsurf0": 260.9120178708837,
      "tbot0": 274.0,
      "z_deep0": 8.0,
      "psisat0": 0.7590000033378601
     },
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.0
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "dsh2o_dt_total",
       "time": 0.0,
       "coords": {
        "lev": 1
       },
       "expected": -3.7509118033796085e-07,
       "tolerance": {
        "abs": 1e-14
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "dsh2o_dt_total",
       "time": 0.0,
       "coords": {
        "lev": 2
       },
       "expected": -2.6423307986078726e-12,
       "tolerance": {
        "abs": 1e-14
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "dsh2o_dt_total",
       "time": 0.0,
       "coords": {
        "lev": 3
       },
       "expected": -3.863829256545159e-08,
       "tolerance": {
        "abs": 1e-14
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "dsh2o_dt_total",
       "time": 0.0,
       "coords": {
        "lev": 4
       },
       "expected": -1.117108905379638e-08,
       "tolerance": {
        "abs": 1e-14
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "dsmc_dt_total",
       "time": 0.0,
       "coords": {
        "lev": 1
       },
       "expected": 1.9240908866180462e-08,
       "tolerance": {
        "abs": 1e-14
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "dsmc_dt_total",
       "time": 0.0,
       "coords": {
        "lev": 2
       },
       "expected": -2.6423307986078726e-12,
       "tolerance": {
        "abs": 1e-14
       }
      },
      {
